Array:
 - An array is a sequence of exactly N elements of the same type. Its length is part of its type.
 - var a [3]int
 - func update(a [3]int) {
        a[0] = 100
    }
    
    func main() {
        a := [3]int{1, 2, 3}
        update(a)
        fmt.Println(a) // [1 2 3]
    }
 - In the above example, it is clear that arrays when passed to a function, copy of the array is received not the pointer

